Z||000027||My7Fieros||05-02-2001||12:44 AM||||Thanx for all the kind words...to answer some questions, the Kumhos are GREAT. They have excellent ratings, and the price is very nice. I ordered them online from discount tire direct I believe.<BR>The paint is called Frost White. Its a Dupont Nason product. Its actually a single stage paint (instead of base coat/clear coat). I usually use the base coat/ clear coat paint, but figured Id try the single stage...I love it!<BR>For added touches we painted mirrors/ground effects and underside of the decklid (pic).<BR>We put new dew wipes on, so taking off the mirror was nec anyway..made for a nice job on the mirrors, and we got to keep the mirror "gasket" or whatever black.<BR>Formula, as far as the red one in the background under the covered parking, that is my Formula that I restored last year. Check the archives for that post w/ the before and after pics (I think it was titled "FORMULA RESTORATION COMPLETE".<BR>The badge behind the wheels idea was kind of an afterthought. I had a few laying around and was trying to figure out what to do w/ them....I may just have to do that on some of my other Fieros as well.<BR>WampusCat, sure, we'll paint yours...email me w/your # and I'll give you a call. Im in Germantown...we'll see what we can do!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> M7F||||reg||7
Z||000028||AkursedX||05-02-2001||01:08 AM||||My rims look EXACTLY the same as yours, right down to the little indentation in the one spoke for whatever lettering you have in there, except that mine only have holes for a 5x100 pattern,  but the funny thing is, mine are Konig Tantrums.  I swear they are exactly the same though.  I will have pics of my car posted this weekend.  <P>Oh yeah, and by the way, it is one very pretty car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
